{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "22", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "10", "M": "11", "S": "23"}}, "news": [{"title": "Patna civic body acts on 26,746 property misuse cases", "para": "Following a Supreme Court directive pertaining to the Loganathan vs State of Tamil Nadu case, the Patna Municipal Corporation is targeting more than 26,000 cases of unauthorized construction. To ensure swift resolution, executive officers will hold periodic hearings, issuing notices to property owners in residential zones. This initiative seeks to uphold compliance and enhance living conditions for residents.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/patna-civic-body-acts-on-26746-property-misuse-cases/133419627?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-154096/133419627.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Ranchi civic body orders installing rainwater harvesting structures on eligible properties", "para": "The Ranchi Municipal Corporation has taken a bold step by mandating the installation of rainwater harvesting systems for qualifying properties. These systems are essential for recharging groundwater, and property owners are obligated to set them up and maintain them properly. Those who fail to comply could face stringent administrative consequences and potential service disconnections.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/ranchi-civic-body-orders-installing-rainwater-harvesting-structures-on-eligible-properties/133419589?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-390098/133419589.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "NCLT removes IRP from stalled Noida project for hiding charges against him", "para": "The NCLT has officially dismissed Narender Kumar Sharma from his role as IRP for the Festival City housing project due to non-disclosure of disciplinary actions and the absence of proper authorization. Sudhir Kumar Agarwal has been appointed as his replacement. It's crucial for Sharma to transfer all project documentation to Agarwal, and any costs incurred during Sharma's administration are excluded from the resolution expenses.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/nclt-removes-irp-from-stalled-noida-project-for-hiding-charges-against-him/133417058?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-43494/133417058.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}